<Item XName="IQGeneration" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>This property enables the user to tell the modulation analysis whether the transmitted signal was generated on-axis (QPSK states have I or Q components) or at 45 degrees (QPSK energy have I and Q components) to ensure that transmitter amplitude imbalance and quadrature error measurements are attributed correctly.  If this information is not known, the property can be safely left at its default value.</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<Enum>WLAN_11ad_EVM__IQGeneration@WLAN 11ad Enums</Enum>
<Range />
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="InterpacketGap" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>InterpacketGap</DataEntry>
<Description>The Inter-packet gap value determines the duration of the zero signal energy period preceding each packet.  The value is limited to 0 to 200 microsecond. The default value is 2 microsecond.</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<HideCondition>1 == FrameLengthOption</HideCondition>
